Subject: [PATCH] i386: call void builtin generators without a destination

The instruction generators in the VOID_FTYPE_VOID group take no operands.
Passing the unused target selects a one-argument indirect call, which
WebAssembly rejects when expanding pause and the other void builtins.

--- a/gcc/config/i386/i386-expand.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/i386/i386-expand.cc
@@ -12052,7 +12052,7 @@
   switch ((enum ix86_builtin_func_type) d->flag)
     {
     case VOID_FTYPE_VOID:
-      emit_insn (GEN_FCN (icode) (target));
+      emit_insn (GEN_FCN (icode) ());
       return 0;
     case VOID_FTYPE_UINT64:
     case VOID_FTYPE_UNSIGNED:
